        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1624a619-1079-5161-9a5b-5f8518974d3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred Döblin, César Vallejo\n- Roles: novelist, essayist, doctor, poet, writer, playwright, journalist, author\n- Works: Berlin Alexanderplatz, Tales of a Long Night, Los heraldos negros\n- Topics: German literature, Peruvian poetry\n\nFacts:\n- Alfred Döblin was born on 10 August 1878 and died on 26 June 1957.\n- César Vallejo was born on 16 March 1892 and died on 15 April 1938.\n- César Vallejo was a Peruvian poet, writer, playwright, and journalist.\n- Between 1915 and 1918, César Vallejo wrote the poems collected in Los heraldos negros.\n- Los heraldos negros was published in July 1919.\n- In 1929, Alfred Döblin published Berlin Alexanderplatz, the novel for which he is best known.\n- Alfred Döblin was a German novelist, essayist, and doctor.\n- Tales of a Long Night, titled Hamlet oder Die lange Nacht nimmt ein Ende in German, was published in 1956.\n- Tales of a Long Night was the last novel by German author Alfred Döblin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
